Let $R$ be a unital ring, and $f : R\rightarrow uRu$ a ring isomorphism, where $u \in R$ is an idempotent and $f(1)=u$. Define
\begin{align}\label{skewcornerring}
R[x,y,f]: = R\langle x, y \rangle / \langle yx=1, xy=u, xr=f(r)x, ry=yf(r) \mid r\in R\rangle. 
\end{align}
The ring $uRu$ is called a \emph{corner ring}, and we refer to $R[x,y,f]$ as a \emph{corner skew Laurent polynomial ring}.
